Subject: Write padding fields as plain blobs rather than opaque-marked ones

With `use_opaque_newtype_wrapper` on, `helpers::blob` wraps the blob it builds
in `__bindgen_marker_Opaque<...>`, which tells a downstream tool that the field
holds a value of some type bindgen could not describe and that its contents are
to be kept out of reach. That is right for an opaque type or an opaque base. It
is not right for padding: the bytes between and after the fields hold no value
at all and any bit pattern is fine in them. Behind the marker, Rust code which
builds such a struct by hand can only fill the padding with the marker's
`Default` and can never read or write it as the bytes it is, and a tool reading
the bindings is told the struct holds opaque data it does not.

Write the padding the struct layout tracker inserts (between fields and at the
tail) and the run between a struct's bases and its first field as the plain
blob `helpers::blob_inner` builds: an integer or an array of them for alignment
up to four, an `__BindgenOpaqueArray` for an array longer than the derive limit
or for alignment above four. Opaque types, opaque bases and union storage keep
the marker.

Based on adetaylor/rust-bindgen#15 by tchebb.

--- a/codegen/mod.rs
+++ b/codegen/mod.rs
@@ -3266,7 +3266,8 @@
                     padding_layout,
                     None,
                 );
-                let ty = helpers::blob(ctx, padding_layout, false);
+                // Padding, not an opaque value: written as the plain blob.
+                let ty = helpers::blob_inner(ctx, padding_layout, false);
                 let access_spec = access_specifier(visibility);
                 fields.push(quote! {
                     #access_spec __bindgen_padding_bases: #ty,
--- a/codegen/struct_layout.rs
+++ b/codegen/struct_layout.rs
@@ -443,7 +443,9 @@
     }
 
     fn padding_field(&mut self, layout: Layout) -> proc_macro2::TokenStream {
-        let ty = helpers::blob(self.ctx, layout, false);
+        // Padding holds no value of the type's, so it is written as the plain
+        // blob, never wrapped as opaque: it can be named and filled by hand.
+        let ty = helpers::blob_inner(self.ctx, layout, false);
         let padding_count = self.padding_count;
 
         self.padding_count += 1;
